#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0163 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC structure=BDS. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), ATOXGR(Char). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | GRADE2`. The mirror of scenario 1: the COMPANION ATOXGR is declared and the CONDITION variable BTOXGR is not, so the first conjunct `var_exists('BTOXGR')` is FALSE and the rule stays silent. This is the DISCRIMINATING direction test - it is the scenario that fails if the two operands are ever swapped. The rule has no wildcard and no scope gate here, so it executes and evaluates FALSE."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ATOXGR type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | GRADE2
